.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR]event\f[R] struct and all its string fields are owned by the
library and are freed after the callback returns.
Copy strings with \f[CR]strdup()\f[R] if they are needed beyond the
callback scope.
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR]seq\f[R] field correlates pre and post events for the same
command execution.
A \f[CR]pre_command\f[R] event with \f[CR]seq=N\f[R] will be followed by
a \f[CR]post_command\f[R] event with the same \f[CR]seq=N\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR]command\f[R] string may be truncated by the server if it
exceeds the maximum event payload size (currently 64 KB).
.IP \(bu 2
Callbacks execute synchronously within \f[CR]bc_poll()\f[R].
Long\-running callbacks delay processing of subsequent messages.
Keep callbacks short and non\-blocking.
.IP \(bu 2
Registering a callback does not automatically subscribe to events.
Call \f[CR]bc_observe_subscribe()\f[R] separately.
.IP \(bu 2
Thread safety: callbacks are always invoked from the thread that calls
\f[CR]bc_poll()\f[R].
The library is not thread\-safe.
